<title>FINLAND: Raisio jumps on U.S. Benecol deal.</title>
<headline>Raisio jumps on U.S. Benecol deal.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Finnish food, animal feed and chemicals group Raision Tehtaat surged nearly 15 percent on Tuesday after it sealed a U.S. deal for the active ingredient of its Benecol cholesterol-cutting margarine.</p>
<p>At 1545/1245 GMT, Raisio traded at 425.10, up 55.10 markka. It was the fifth most actively traded share by turnover.  </p>
<p>After 15 minutes, Raisio was up 79.00 markka or over 21 percent at 449.00 with one broker seeing it testing 450.</p>
<p>The broker added that the jump in Raisio's stock was to the extent of Helsinki bourse limits at 15 percent: that had slowed initial offers.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +3589 6805 0247, e-mail news@reuters.fi</p>
